"What? The Sun Spirit...?"{w}{p}"That... might be something really serious, huh?"{w}{p}"If the Sun Spirit kicks the bucket, the world'll be
swallowed up in darkness."{w}{p}"And then everything'll go just the way
that bunch wants."{w}{p}"I'll ask around on my end.{w}You lot keep up the investigation."{w}{p}"Right then. I'm counting on you."{w}

"Plenty of adventurers have already
got their compasses and set out, you know."{w}{p}"If you don't want to get beaten to it,
you'd better hurry to Algrantz Castle."{w}

"Oh, you got your compass!
Alrighty, let the adventure begin!
Now off you go -- ZOOM!{w}

"A spear can thrust, slash and sweep, but
it really comes down to two: ZABANG and SHABASHOOM.{w}And even thrusts come in ZABANG, ZUNK, all sorts..."{w}{p}"Then there are two big ways to cut with a blade!
ZANG and ZAGANG. Katana and sword, basically.{w}

{0E}"Then there are two big ways to cut with a blade!
ZANG and ZAGANG. Katana and sword, basically.{0F}
...Hm? It's easier to follow this way?"{w}

"Oh, it's you guys... Hey, there's something I want to ask you.
Is stuff like WHAM and SHZAK... hard to follow?{w}But WHAM is WHAM, right...? Mutter, mutter..."{w}{p}"...Lately people say their instructor talks in
the language of another world. Is it really that bad?{w}But real combat isn't about logic... is it?"{w}

{0E}"But a king can't act -- it'd start a war.
So I'll protect lots of people in the King's place.{0F}
We'll do what the King couldn't do -- all of us, okay?"{w}

{0E}"Mmf, nngh... This cake is quite something!
As expected of that patissier............?{0F}
What might you want, one wonders? I am on duty, so I am."{w}

{0E}"Mmf, nom... This town has grown prosperous indeed.
This baked treat! The contrast in texture between outside and inside...!{0F}
Hm? Oh, it's you chaps. Would you chaps care for one?"{w}{p}"Why am I eating so much, would you suppose?{w}...*Gulp*{w}This is important verification work, to learn how the people live."{w}{p}"Where do you chaps think prosperity shows itself?{w}In amusements.{w}Above all, it shows itself in luxuries, so it does."{w}

"Mmf, nngh... Mmm-hmm, so it is.{w}Oh, it's you chaps. Would you chaps...
happen to know of any unusual sweets, would you suppose?"{w}{p}"I see, you do not know, then...{w}Of late, the sweets of this town have changed little,
and I find myself growing a tad bored, so I do..."{w}

"A lack of variety leads to poverty of the heart!
It is a crisis for the nation, would you suppose!
I am counting on you, so I aaam!"{w}

"At any rate, you were a great help this time, would you suppose.{w}You chaps, with such a keen eye for sweets,
are surely people I can trust, would you suppose."{w}{p}"From now on, whenever you chaps have business at the palace,
you must come to me, would you suppose.{w}Leave it to me, so it iiis!"{w}

"Plants seem like they grow all by themselves, right?{w}If all you want is for them to grow, that works fine."{w}{p}"But if you want them to look beautiful,
you've got to put in the effort."{w}{p}"This'll sound strange, but
I can sort of hear what plants are saying.{w}Not that they actually talk, mind you."{w}

"As for me... well, actually,
I've got a bit of a problem...{w}If you've got the time, I'd like you to hear me out."{w}{p}"See, I got hold of this strange little sapling.
Could you take a look at it, just once?"{w}
